---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Dnaso privacy policy: what data we collect, how Google AdSense and analytics use cookies, and your choices."
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: October 19, 2026</em></p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>Dnaso is a static informational website. We don't run accounts, comments, newsletters, or contact forms that store your data. If you email us, we keep your message only long enough to respond.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
    <p>We use <strong>Google AdSense</strong> to serve ads. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this and other sites. Specifically:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google uses the <strong>DoubleClick cookie</strong> to serve interest-based ads.</li>
      <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
      <li>You can opt out of some third-party vendors' cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info/choices</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Learn more in Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">how Google uses data from partner sites</a>.</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>We use privacy-respecting, cookie-free page-view analytics to understand which guides are useful. No personal data is collected or sold.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Our guides link to manufacturer sites and other resources. Their privacy practices are their own.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes materially, we'll update the date above. Continued use of the site means you accept the current version.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Privacy questions: <strong>hello@dnaso.com</strong></p>
  </div>
</Base>
